    reading: mu2 >= s2 (Ritz is an upper bound) => theta(mu2) >= theta(s2): the estimate can only
             push the certificate UP (over-claim).  It can also land BELOW s2 with a bad basis, so
             no GEVP/Ritz/rho^2 estimate controls s2 in the direction the certificate needs (below).
             rho^2*s1 tracks s2 only in the near-harmonic regime; at g=100 it is off by orders.
