(G) beta=0 Haar: degenerate level => N-state band criterion
    SU(2) Haar: Var((1/2)tr U) = 0.2500  (exact 1/4)  => M0 finite at beta=0
    beta=0: T = |1><1| (rank one) => every excitation at s = infinity: nu = delta_infinity,
            no (s1,s2,Ebar) at all => the bridge is UNDEFINED (an inf/inf, not a 0/0).
    regularised: N states spread uniformly over a band of width W => eps=W/(N-1), Ebar-s1=eps(N-1)/2
                 theta = (3-N)/2  (independent of W);  theta>0 needs N<=2
      N=    2: eps=1.000e+00  theta=+0.5000  (w1=0.5000)
      N=    3: eps=5.000e-01  theta=+0.0000  (w1=0.3333)
      N=    4: eps=3.333e-01  theta=-0.5000  (w1=0.2500)
      N=    8: eps=1.429e-01  theta=-2.5000  (w1=0.1250)
      N=  100: eps=1.010e-02  theta=-48.5000  (w1=0.0100)
      N= 1000: eps=1.001e-03  theta=-498.5000  (w1=0.0010)
    => few-level certificate: N states in the low band give theta = (3-N)/2 <= 0 for N>=3.
       free field / beta=0 / any cut: N -> infinity => theta -> -infinity.  No certificate.
